{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A form error with no aria-live or role attribute might be perfectly visible and still be completely silent to a screen reader user — the visual fix isn't automatically the accessible fix.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Render an empty aria-live="polite" container in the form's initial markup and only write the error text into it afterward — that ordering is what makes the announcement reliable.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Reserve role="alert" (assertive) for errors the user must not miss right now, like a failed payment, and keep routine field validation on aria-live="polite" so it doesn't interrupt whatever they're still doing.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
